    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Jackson Merrill** serving as our primary offensive catalysts. **Gunnar Henderson** draws a prime matchup against V\u00e1squez (4.89 xERA) and benefits from an elite park factor (+16%) and a high-leverage lineup spot, pushing his score to an impressive 81.88. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance against Gibson; the combination of a favorable 5.87 xERA and a generous +16% park adjustment elevates him to a score of 75.27. Both players offer the perfect blend of hitting environment and projectable run production needed to climb the 5x5 standings.\n\nThe optimization process was tightest at the utility spot, where **Nasim Nunez** (50.40) narrowly held off **Nolan Schanuel** (44.14). While **Nolan Schanuel** provides a solid floor, the scarcity of speed in our league architecture keeps **Nasim Nunez** in the mix despite his unfavorable #9 spot in the order. Elsewhere, we are cautious regarding **Sam Antonacci** and **Wade Meckler**, both of whom face high-skill arms in Yamamoto and Griffin Jax, respectively. Their scores are suppressed by these SP matchups, necessitating a \"wait and see\" approach. \n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding **Jacob Wilson**, as his 62.50 score is contingent upon the official confirmation of his #5 lineup slot. Any move lower in the order could jeopardize his efficiency rating. Furthermore, while we monitor the health status of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, we are comfortable with our depth; we considered **Miguel Vargas** for a start today, but his matchup against the elite Yamamoto (-16% SP skill adjustment) made him the odd man out, falling short of our 40-point threshold for active play.",
